00:21:34.300 --> 00:21:35.260
Tell her yes.

00:21:36.010 --> 00:21:36.830
He says yes.

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:39.550
Well, make him wait there till I've looked at his feet.

00:21:42.010 --> 00:21:43.760
Violet, I have to go, dear.

00:21:44.120 --> 00:21:45.020
I've got the electric.

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:52.190
Oh, I'm so sorry.

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:53.910
I've been thinking about my sister.

00:21:54.070 --> 00:21:55.750
She seems to have had a rather active holiday.

00:21:57.180 --> 00:21:58.160
The shoes.

00:21:58.900 --> 00:21:59.680
You room.

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:01.820
but I'll proceed you from last time.

00:22:02.860 --> 00:22:03.660
Very well.

00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:06.160
Well, leave them outside and do come in.

00:22:07.430 --> 00:22:08.030
Thank you, dear.

00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:12.290
Great implement on the one I had before.

00:22:13.480 --> 00:22:15.020
He used to brush against my walls.

00:22:15.630 --> 00:22:17.150
Of course, I rang his superiors.

00:22:17.210 --> 00:22:17.930
I told him, I said,

00:22:18.050 --> 00:22:21.270
I will not have electric men brushing against my walls.

00:22:23.660 --> 00:22:24.980
Elizabeth, close the door, dear.

00:22:25.080 --> 00:22:25.600
The heat's on.

00:22:27.200 --> 00:22:29.620
Ah, oh, fingers.

00:22:30.060 --> 00:22:36.160
Eight, three, two, one.

00:22:39.060 --> 00:22:51.230
As it was, do you think?

00:22:51.720 --> 00:22:54.080
My pots are sometimes very difficult to clean.

00:22:54.630 --> 00:22:55.630
Cleanest fuel there is.

00:22:56.090 --> 00:22:57.730
It goes to some very funny families.

00:22:58.160 --> 00:22:59.980
Would you have mine checked to make quite sure...

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:00.680
I get it first.

00:23:00.860 --> 00:23:02.060
Leave it with me, lady.

00:23:02.960 --> 00:23:04.080
Because I won't have it

00:23:04.080 --> 00:23:04.980
if it's already been

00:23:04.980 --> 00:23:06.120
to some of those other places.

00:23:07.340 --> 00:23:08.140
Right, old madam.

00:23:08.500 --> 00:23:09.200
Much obliged.

00:23:16.720 --> 00:23:26.200
Be it's only I, dear.

00:23:27.080 --> 00:23:28.240
Especially when you're shouting

00:23:28.240 --> 00:23:29.380
at where the neighbours can hear.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:30.880
I'm not sure.

00:23:31.320 --> 00:23:33.240
Well, neither am I, so you must be careful.

00:23:34.570 --> 00:23:35.290
How's your father?

00:23:36.190 --> 00:23:37.830
Rang, the ward sister answered.

00:23:38.490 --> 00:23:40.650
She says he's sitting up and beginning to take an interest.

00:23:40.910 --> 00:23:41.610
Oh, that's good.

00:23:41.930 --> 00:23:43.070
In the physiotherapist.

00:23:45.470 --> 00:23:48.590
He thinks he's in love with the physiotherapist.

00:23:49.680 --> 00:23:51.140
Probably just the drugs.

00:23:51.670 --> 00:23:55.470
And that swine Bruce wants my sister to wear some awful leather outfit.

00:23:56.600 --> 00:23:58.560
Is she going to take her motorcycling?

00:23:59.420 --> 00:23:59.980
No, it's not.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:03.180
It's not motorcycling. It's something he picked up in Spain.

00:24:04.900 --> 00:24:05.300
Bullfighting.

00:24:05.440 --> 00:24:06.720
No, don't think it's that either.

00:24:07.870 --> 00:24:10.870
Anyway, dear, enough of my problems. Did you manage to get my parsley?

00:24:11.270 --> 00:24:14.470
Yes, in the kitchen. And you'll never guess who I bumped into.

00:24:14.770 --> 00:24:17.310
Good. Would you polish those glasses for me, dear?

00:24:18.150 --> 00:24:20.880
And then give me a hand with buffing up the cruet.

00:24:26.890 --> 00:24:27.690
Well done.

00:24:28.740 --> 00:24:29.960
How sensitive of you.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:36.280
you to call dear. What a close psychic link we have you and I. What does he want? I don't

00:24:36.280 --> 00:24:43.780
know that he wants anything. He's just ringing his mother. You need how much Sheridan? For

00:24:43.780 --> 00:24:49.760
what? You've joined an organisation. Well that's nice dear. Making friends. What kind

00:24:49.760 --> 00:24:56.100
of an organisation? Is it like a club? A golf club? Not a golf club. I see. Just a group

00:24:56.100 --> 00:24:59.760
of friends. You call yourselves what dear?

00:25:01.050 --> 00:25:02.470
The sword of the people.

00:25:02.690 --> 00:25:04.130
Now, do be careful, Sheridan.

00:25:04.710 --> 00:25:06.680
Make sure they're not too sharp.

00:25:09.140 --> 00:25:10.420
Always wear a mask.

00:25:11.480 --> 00:25:12.460
You do wear masks.

00:25:12.640 --> 00:25:13.640
Oh, that's very sensible.

00:25:16.040 --> 00:25:17.520
You'll pay daddy back when?

00:25:18.930 --> 00:25:20.670
When you've robbed your first bank, Sheridan.

00:25:21.970 --> 00:25:25.990
Look, dear, find some nice philatelic society to join.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:39.320
will not send a check. Richard, that's Sheridan on the phone. Now listen, Sheridan, you've

00:25:39.320 --> 00:25:49.360
upset your father. Oh, Richard, I'm so sorry. I was expecting another call. Yes. Oh, yes,

00:25:49.480 --> 00:25:54.080
my candlelight supper is still on. Oh, it's been a funny day, but we have to press on.

00:25:55.400 --> 00:25:59.910
Would I look some flows from your conservatory? How very kind.

00:26:00.090 --> 00:26:06.450
This'll pop along now. That's very civilised of you, Major. Bye!

00:26:07.830 --> 00:26:08.830
What about Sheridan?

00:26:09.560 --> 00:26:10.620
Don't send him any money.

00:26:31.050 --> 00:26:41.640
It's delightful. You know, this is so kind of you.

00:26:43.330 --> 00:26:45.610
I've got some prime blooms for you.

00:26:45.830 --> 00:26:46.950
Oh, lovely.

00:26:49.220 --> 00:26:51.020
You'll have all of it yourself.

00:26:51.520 --> 00:26:52.360
It's a special.

00:26:53.190 --> 00:26:54.350
Oh, oh, no.

00:26:56.170 --> 00:26:57.870
I lost the pressure.

00:26:58.270 --> 00:26:59.310
I lost it.

00:27:01.150 --> 00:27:01.350
Thank you.

00:27:35.310 --> 00:27:36.110
What's wrong now?

00:27:37.100 --> 00:27:42.680
Nothing is wrong. As far as anyone is concerned, nothing is wrong.

00:27:43.540 --> 00:27:47.610
We're going to have a candlelight supper. It's going to be the usual success.

00:27:49.000 --> 00:27:53.080
I see no reason for trailing our problems in front of our friends.

00:27:53.790 --> 00:27:55.090
Is the Major coming?

00:27:56.050 --> 00:27:59.460
Yes, Richard. I do believe the Major.

00:28:00.350 --> 00:28:01.490
Will be coming.

00:28:02.990 --> 00:28:04.530
And it's a good job he is a major.

00:28:05.400 --> 00:28:08.120
If he was a sergeant, he wouldn't get a foot past the door.

00:29:01.150 --> 00:29:01.470
Thank you.
